It *will* tend to move toward you, however each single move that a pet
will make will be in a random direction. In this case there is only two
possible ways to move, so naturally the risk of the pet moving to the
next trap is 50%. After that it's 100% as then there is traps on both
sides. Even if it comes out of the trap, there's still a 50% chance of
it immediately going back into it. As I said, just an easy way to kill
off your pet.




